+# Receipts stopped
+
+For the volunteer on call when members report that no receipt emails arrive. Brings receipts back by restarting the
+worker and letting it send the jobs that queued while it was down; while the worker is down, no member gets a receipt.
+The cause so far has been a deploy: the deploy script restarts the web app but not the
+[worker](../architecture.md#parts), so the worker stays stopped after it. Written after September 14, the second time
+this happened: the first time nobody else knew the fix and members waited until noon. Owner: Tomás.
+
+## Before you begin
+
+- A shell on the server, with `sudo` for `systemctl`.
+- `psql` access to the `larder` database.
+
+## Steps
+
+1. Check the worker: `systemctl status larder-worker`.
+
+   Expected: `inactive (dead)`, usually since just after the last deploy. If it says `active (running)`, the worker is
+   not the cause: go to [If it fails](#if-it-fails).
+2. Count the waiting jobs: `psql larder -c "select status, count(*) from procrastinate_jobs group by status"`.
+
+   Expected: a `todo` count that grew while the worker was down (212 after one night on September 14), `doing` at 0,
+   and a few `failed`. Note the `todo` and `failed` counts.
+3. Start the worker: `sudo systemctl start larder-worker`.
+
+   Expected: `systemctl status larder-worker` says `active (running)`.
+4. A minute later, run the query of step 2 again, and repeat until `todo` reaches 0.
+
+   Expected: `todo` falls by about 40 a minute and reaches 0; 212 jobs took under 10 minutes.
+5. Compare the `failed` count with the one you noted in step 2.
+
+   Expected: it has not grown. The few failed jobs that were already there are receipts that bounced because the
+   member has no valid email address; leave them.
+
+## If it fails
+
+If the worker stops again right after you start it, read its last log lines:
+`journalctl -u larder-worker -n 50`, and post them to Tomás in #larder-ops. Do the same if the worker was running but
+receipts still do not arrive, or if `failed` keeps growing.
